<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhine Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1822–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rhenish Prussia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> Province was a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, formed in 1822 from lands on both banks of the Rhine that Prussia gained at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a> as its capital. It absorbed many former ecclesiastical states, imperial cities and small principalities, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> became its largest city. It was divided after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhine-province.jpg" alt="Rhine Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Preu%C3%9Fen_-_Rheinland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
